{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789913714,"nonce":"/2kY/DmT7/Oxxma0zb59DdcbNGk=","title":"Lua: start-up and whole-process wall time","message":"The bench runner reports elapsed and wall; the gap is about 65 ms on fib (96 ms wall against 25 ms elapsed). ZYNTAX_TRACE_LOWER_PHASES puts it at: the in-process `library()` typing pass 5 to 17 ms, runtime construction 0.5 to 11 ms, program compile 21 to 57 ms. LuaJIT's whole process on fib is 23 ms.\n\nThe library's typed declarations belong in the snapshot with its HIR, not rebuilt from the Builtin tables at every start. Program compile latency is the remaining term: measure which passes run on a small chunk and what the tiered runtime compiles eagerly. Related: load costs 25 ms a chunk (63840a4).","files":null}]}